.worktrees/
.superpowers/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
build/
.claude/

# Internal-audience conference/handoff docs, not meant for the public repo.
docs/analytics-handoff.md
docs/architecture-talk-slides.md
docs/hitcon-2026-workshop.html
# data/* not data/ — git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded,
# so excluding the directory itself would make the negation below silently do nothing.
data/*
*.db
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The one exception, and it must come after *.db to win: the frozen 182-alert graded
# corpus every benchmark result was measured against. Committing the evidence without
# its input leaves the findings unreproducible from a clone. Self-authored synthetic
# logs only — seeded from wazuh_deployment/single-node/, no real alert data.
!data/bench_alerts.db

# Benchmark evidence IS committed — the reports, per-run records, gate results and
# sweep logs are what the findings in docs/PROGRESS.md rest on, and they cannot be
# regenerated without ~20 hours of model time.
#
# Two exclusions, both regenerable working state rather than evidence:
#   - each block copies the corpus snapshot and mutates it as it runs (alert status,
#     persisted reports); the reports are exported as JSON alongside, so the copy
#     carries nothing the committed files do not. 23 copies, 20MB of the 26MB total.
#   - *.db above already excludes them; this is the explicit note about why.
bench/results/**/alerts.db
